ision, leadership, but not good at taking criticism, unorganized. No explicit reliability, stress, etc.\n\nGiven the criteria, reliability is crucial. Candidate C is 100% reliable, B is very conscientious (reliability). Both strong. Cooperation: C creates positive atmosphere, B can be uncooperative. So C may be better on crew cooperation. Decision quality: C quick correct decisions, B unknown. Stress: B handles stress well, D adequate, A unknown, C unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, spatial vision; B good at weather, computer; D solves problems; C unknown.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously; A leadership; B conscientious; C puts concern for others above everything? Actually not in notes but earlier mention? Not in our notes. So D strong.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate best overall. Perhaps Candidate C offers reliability and crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be problematic. However positive atmosphere suggests good crew cooperation despite difficulty communicating? Might be contradictory.\n\nCandidate B's uncooperative may be more severe.\n\nMaybe we can argue that Candidate C's reliability and positive crew atmosphere outweigh communication issues, and that his quick decision making is valuable. So we could shift recommendation to C.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 2 noted B's cooperation concerns, but also said B's strengths. We can say that after reviewing C's 100% reliability and positive crew atmosphere, I think C may be stronger overall.\n\nWe need to use explicit facts: C is 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, can make correct decisions quickly. Also note difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric as concerns.\n\nThus we can propose Candidate C as current recommendation.\n\nWe must output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\".\n\nLet's craft message: \"I appreciate Agent 2's points, but I think C's reliability and crew atmosphere tip